diff --git a/HANDOFF.md b/HANDOFF.md
index f99e7661465af1b9767cb3478e41c634d4a4eed6..65b78465895d8cd387d0c10864729a04b42853a5 100644
--- a/HANDOFF.md
+++ b/HANDOFF.md
@@ -7,8 +7,8 @@ Upstream CoopDX baseline: `6bfcfede7a5c1af400daa269931a9ae13ed157ad`
 
 Mission 01 added an iOS Files ZIP picker and production-importer ZIP preflight, and preserved root-level Lua archive naming. No renderer source was changed or copied.
 
-Mission 02 has begun with `METAL_INTEGRATION_PLAN.md`, `RENDERER_PARITY.md`, and `VALIDATION.md`. Key constraint: CoopDX's `GfxRenderingAPI` receives full `ColorCombiner*` values; the previous iOS Metal implementation takes packed 32-bit IDs, so direct casting/hash mapping is invalid. Implement a new semantic MSL adapter under the CoopDX interface. Keep OpenGL ES and CoopDX's RSP/display-list/DynOS frontends.
+Mission 02 has a tested semantic combiner-to-MSL generator (`src/pc/gfx/gfx_metal_coopdx_shader.c`) and an iOS-only Objective-C Metal `GfxRenderingAPI` implementation plus SDL Metal layer selection. Metal is opt-in in the display settings; OpenGL ES is still the default. Initialization and built-in pipeline-precompile failures recover to OpenGL ES. These backend changes are source-only until an Apple build runs.
 
 The upstream iOS and Metal renderer roots have no project-level license grant identified. No renderer code has been copied. The local Metal reference remote's SSH fetch failed due a system SSH config permission error; HTTPS confirms its remote `mission-81-shader64-rendergraph` at `259bcaa19ab5c7cd39dab28f1080a650e5739a4c`. The existing local Metal worktree is on `mission-55-6-codemagic` with a pre-existing modified `src/game/skybox.c`; the Mission 81 worktree has pre-existing untracked `--repo`; Mission 82 has pre-existing gameplay/runtime modifications. All were left untouched.
 
-Next: implement and test a portable full-`ColorCombiner` MSL source generator, then integrate it into a fresh iOS backend and SDL Metal surface while retaining GL fallback. Linux builds do not validate UIKit/Metal code. iOS build/IPA/device validation remains pending Xcode/macOS runner access.
+Current commit: `36fd9adb` (combiner adapter); backend and SDL integration are uncommitted at handoff. The next step is to review/fix the Objective-C backend and its color/texture semantics, then validate with the proper pinned SDL2 dependency on a macOS/Xcode runner. The local checkout has no `lib/SDL2-source`, no `xcodebuild`/`xcrun`, and no personal Git remote configured, so it cannot currently produce or publish an iOS build. Do not push to `upstream`.
diff --git a/METAL_INTEGRATION_PLAN.md b/METAL_INTEGRATION_PLAN.md
index 1ce21b7d310fe101605e53f5879b271c8efd1f31..913faa1492d6872262f09896a8c55fff2f33e42e 100644
--- a/METAL_INTEGRATION_PLAN.md
+++ b/METAL_INTEGRATION_PLAN.md
@@ -36,3 +36,11 @@ The inspected CoopDX iOS and `sm64ios-metal` repository roots do not contain a p
 3. Add SDL Metal surface/present integration and restart-required backend choice, retaining OpenGL ES fallback.
 4. Validate combiner/state behavior with host tests and Apple Metal shader compilation; build on a macOS runner before claiming iOS compilation.
 5. Exercise vanilla rendering, then DynOS/custom assets and Lua-driven graphics behavior. Defer post-processing and other effects until vanilla parity.
+
+## Current implementation checkpoint
+
+- A portable C generator now translates the CoopDX combiner commands to MSL and computes a canonical key from all combiner values, flags, input mapping, and commands. Its host tests cover the generated shader shape, key equality and vertex layout.
+- An iOS Objective-C Metal backend has been added behind `GfxRenderingAPI`. It creates pipelines from the generated MSL, uploads RGBA textures, binds two tiles, implements depth/blend/decal/viewport/scissor state, and submits the frontend's triangle batches. GPU texture memory and per-batch vertex memory are bounded.
+- SDL now creates a Metal view/layer when Metal is selected. The display menu offers OpenGL ES and Metal on iOS. OpenGL ES remains the default and Metal initialization or built-in shader precompile errors trigger a restart-free initialization fallback to OpenGL ES.
+- The backend is currently **source implemented, not Apple compiled**. Runtime combiner variants used after startup can still fail independently; that path logs a diagnostic but does not hot-switch renderers. Full rendering parity is not claimed. Unsupported details are recorded in `RENDERER_PARITY.md`.
+- iOS CMake/IPA validation is blocked locally by the absent `lib/SDL2-source` directory and absent Xcode/iOS SDK tools. Do not use the current source checkpoint as a device-test build until those prerequisites are restored and Apple compilation succeeds.
